  "name": "prioritizing-my-inbox",
  "description": "Build a personal, ranked shortlist of the PostHog Inbox reports the current user is most likely to care about right now. Combines the user's activity summary (what they work on and keep an eye on), the inbox ranking model's open, action and fix probabilities and lifts, suggested-reviewer routing, ownership, pull request state and recency, then returns the top N (25 by default) ordered from most to least relevant. Use when the user says \"let's look at my inbox\", \"what's in my inbox for me?\", \"my top 10 inbox reports\", \"what should I look at today?\", or asks to re-rank, focus, or filter that list. For browsing, filtering, drilling into, or acting on a single report, use `inbox-exploration`.",
